  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1/3. Two DUT bugs fixed: (1) issue0_2 arbitration (line 51): inverted qAge(2) age comparison in issue0_2's slot2-vs-slot1 priority — changed `(qAge(2) | ~io.opsReady(1))` to `(~qAge(2) | ~io.opsReady(1))`, so slot2 defers to slot1 when slot1 is older. (2) qAge update logic (lines 72-76): each qAge bit persisted even when the younger slot's next-state valid was 0, violating age-consistency assertions; changed from `(~nvJ | qAge(I) | ~valid(J))` to `(nvI & nvJ & (qAge(I) | ~valid(J)))` requiring both related slots to be valid next cycle. Expected effect: resolves issue0_one_hot0, issue1_one_hot0 (mutex), all three age-consistency assertions, and downstream liveness failures caused by arbitration deadlock.",
    "Repair round 2/3. Fixed `issue1_2` age-priority arbitration bug: changed `(qAge(2) | ~io.opsReady(1) | issue0_1)` to `(~qAge(2) | ~io.opsReady(1) | issue0_1)` on the `issue1_2` signal definition. When `qAge(2)=1` (slot1 older than slot2), the original code unconditionally allowed slot2 to issue to exec unit 1 even when slot1 was ready and not already issued to unit 0, causing `io.issue1` to have two bits high (both slot1 and slot2), violating `issue1_one_hot0`. The fix mirrors the homologous correction already applied to `issue0_2` in round 1 — both are slot2-vs-slot1 age comparisons where the complement form `~qAge(2)` is required because slot2 has a higher index than slot1. Expected effect: resolves `issue1_one_hot0` and may also resolve liveness failures (slot forward_progress and ready_eventually_issues) that were caused by the arbitration logic allowing incorrect dual-issue patterns or priority inversions. All assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
    "Round 3/3. DUT bug fix for 6 remaining liveness failures (slot{0,1,2}_forward_progress and slot{0,1,2}_ready_eventually_issues). Root cause: issue-priority age conditions `(qAge(I) | ~opsReady(J))` in all 6 issue signals (issue0_0, issue0_1, issue0_2, issue1_0, issue1_1, issue1_2) did not account for invalid younger slots. When slot J was invalid but opsReady(J)=1 (valid input from testbench), the condition `~opsReady(J)=0` blocked the current slot from issuing even though no instruction existed in slot J to compete. Fix: added `| ~valid(J)` to each age-condition clause across all 6 issue signals (12 clauses total). This allows an older slot to issue past an invalid younger slot regardless of that slot's opsReady value. The `valid(J)` gate directly checks slot occupancy, preventing the false arbitration stall demonstrated in the t=70ns waveform where valid(2)=0 but opsReady(2)=1 blocked issue0_0. All assertion labels preserved unchanged."
